@page "/components/chart"

<PageTitle>Chart — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Chart</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    The useful half of <code>ChartContainer</code>: one custom property per series, so whatever
    draws and whatever labels read the same colour from one place. What draws is yours.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">
    The rest of upstream's component is a wall of <code>[&amp;_.recharts-*]</code> selectors for a
    library this port does not ship. Reach for a real charting library when you need axes, zoom or
    a line through irregular time — it renders inside this and reads the same properties. Until
    then a <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> with a percentage height per bar reads to a screen reader,
    prints, and needs nothing loaded.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="ChartExample.razor"><ChartExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Tooltip</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Recharts draws a floating tooltip onto a canvas nothing else can read. A table already has
    one — the browser's own <code>title</code>, plus the number in the DOM where a screen reader,
    a print stylesheet and Find in Page can all reach it.
</p>
